EspoCRM 10.0.11
  Image:   images/espocrm (built by the runtime image workflow; digest pinned in manifest.yaml)
  Release: https://www.espocrm.com/downloads/EspoCRM-10.0.11.zip
           sha256 cdd04f7efa52a59025ef824c75b06e0a84cf986724a8c5bc4b56fcd2ce8e0ab1
  License: GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 or later (AGPL-3.0-or-later). Full text,
           verbatim from the release: LICENSES/espocrm-10.0.11-LICENSE.txt
           Additional term under AGPLv3 section 7(b), from every EspoCRM source file: the
           Appropriate Legal Notices in the user interface must retain the display of the
           "EspoCRM" word. Sealed does not change EspoCRM's user interface.
  Source:  https://github.com/espocrm/espocrm/tree/10.0.11
           (tag 10.0.11, commit 32d559ba86d3be607599d1325c359668c1178850)

  AGPL section 13: Sealed runs the EspoCRM release unmodified. The image only removes the web
  installer (install/ and public/install/) and moves data/, custom/ and client/custom/ into
  volumes; settings are applied through EspoCRM's own override files at start. The
  corresponding source is the upstream tag above plus catalog/apps/crm/images/espocrm in this
  repository.

  Bundled third-party code in the release: 117 Composer packages (105 MIT, 3 BSD-3-Clause,
  3 BSD-2-Clause, 1 Apache-2.0, 1 MIT OR Apache-2.0, 4 LGPL, per vendor/composer/installed.json;
  the image build fails on any other license) and the front-end libraries in client/lib (jQuery,
  Backbone, Handlebars, Ace and others, under MIT, BSD and Apache-2.0 headers).

  Enterprise code: none. The release contains one module (Crm). EspoCRM's paid extensions are
  separate downloads that are not in the image, and extension uploads from the admin panel are
  turned off.

Runtime from Debian trixie packages (snapshot.debian.org 20261027T000000Z)
  Apache httpd 2.4 (Apache-2.0), PHP 8.4 with mod_php (PHP-3.01; the Zend Engine part is under
  the Zend Engine License 2.00), Node.js 20 (MIT) for the bootstrap job, and their libraries.
  These are OS distribution packages (decisions D-021, D-050). License texts are in each
  package's /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright inside the image, and the release SBOM
  (sbom/espocrm.spdx.json) lists every package. PHP upstream accepted relicensing PHP and the
  Zend Engine under BSD-3-Clause for a later PHP 8 release (https://wiki.php.net/rfc/php_license_update).

